    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking for some advice on pallet stacking for a new high-density racking setup we're installing at our Rotterdam facility. We deal with heavy industrial loads. What's the best way to handle the center of gravity and interlocking patterns to make sure the stacks stay stable when they're high up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For heavy, high-density loads in racking, ensure your stacks are always centered perfectly on the pallet to keep the center of gravity as close to the stack base as possible. Utilize a brick-laying or interlocking pattern when stacking multiple pallets to distribute weight evenly and prevent individual stacks from shifting against each other. Always check the manufacturer's load ratings and racking specifications for maximum height and weight limitations. Proper use of load-bearing plastic or wooden spacers between pallets can also help maintain structural integrity.",
