    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. We're also worried about the stability during the actual movement phase. Sometimes when the forklifts are moving fast or turning corners, the loads seem to shift or vibrate a bit more than they should. Are there specific ways to secure the load or reinforced patterns that help prevent that kind of sudden shifting during transit?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To mitigate shifting and vibration during forklift transit, prioritizing load containment is key. Use stretch wrap or shrink wrap tightly around the entire palletized unit to create a rigid, singular block. Furthermore, if the load permits, bracing the stacks with perpendicular lumber supports can significantly increase lateral stability. Carefully configuring your forklift travel paths to maintain consistent, controlled acceleration and turning speeds will also minimize dynamic forces on the stack.",
      "source": "target",
