      "content": "Sudden, unexpected instability often stems from subtle environmental or procedural factors. Regularly inspect your racking structure for any signs of metal fatigue, bent uprights, or level floor imperfections that could introduce unevenness. Additionally, ensure your wrapping technique accounts for the load's individual features; bulky or irregularly shaped items need more point-specific banding or blocking than uniform items. Finally, proper forklift mast extension and secure carriage positioning are crucial to prevent minor jolts that translate into major load movement.",
